At Sun, 27 Nov 2005 18:39:49 -0800,
Nikhil Rao wrote:
> 
> Hello,
>  
> I am developing a driver for a card that supports unsigned big endian 16 bit format.
> To enable this to work
> with the wav file format (S16LE), I want to use the pcm plugin for format conversion.
>  
> Is this possible to do without mmap  support in the driver ?
>  
> When I had disabled mmap in the info field in the snd_pcm_hardware_t structure, ALSA
> quits with the message
> "unable to find an usable access for plughw:1,1"
>  
> when I enable mmap in the info field, the driver gets called but the code crashes
> since mmap is not supported.

You can set mmap_emulation option in pcm hw definition.
It might be buggy since it's not debugged for a long time, though.


> Please let me know if I need to provide more information.
>  
> I am working with ALSA version 1.0.6.

It's way too old.  I recommend you to use a newer version.


Takashi


